disease-microscope-stage = Stage { $stage } of { $stages }
disease-microscope-genome-complete = The genome is fully assembled
disease-microscope-genome-done = { $stage }. { $symptom }
disease-microscope-genome-current = { $stage }. Pick the stage symptom
disease-microscope-genome-locked = { $stage }. Locked
disease-microscope-rule-growth = Stage quota: { $growth } target cells.
disease-microscope-rule-share = Required field share: at least { $share }% of living cells must be yours.
disease-microscope-rule-moves = The rival answers { $moves } times per move of yours.
disease-microscope-rule-cost = Cost per drop: EZ nutrient { $nutrient }, phenol { $inhibitor }.
disease-microscope-rule-sterile = The inhibitor scorches the medium: nothing ever grows on treated cells again.
disease-microscope-rule-spore = A fully scorched rival sprouts again from a spore elsewhere: it can be held back, never wiped out.
disease-microscope-rule-displace = The rival displaces target cells where the colonies meet.
disease-microscope-rule-cross = The target only grows along the cross of the drop, the rival across the whole area.
disease-microscope-rule-resilient = A rival cell survives the inhibitor while two of its own cells outside the area hold it.
disease-microscope-rule-narrow = The inhibitor hits a five-cell cross instead of a square.
disease-microscope-rule-toxin = Near the quota the rival starts poisoning the medium in front of the target.
disease-microscope-target = Stage target
disease-microscope-prepare = Plate the field
disease-microscope-prepare-hint = Plating the field: { $cost } u of EZ nutrient. The other stage symptom becomes the rival.
disease-microscope-forecast = Forecast ({ $left })
disease-microscope-forecast-active = The forecast is paid for and lasts until your next move: hover a drop over the field to see the rival's reply.
disease-microscope-tool-nutrient = Nutrient
disease-microscope-tool-inhibitor = Inhibitor
disease-microscope-hint-forecast = Phenol, { $cost } u. Stains the smear: until your next move the drop preview also shows the rival's reply. Left this match: { $left }.
disease-microscope-hint-nutrient = EZ nutrient, { $cost } u. Grows both colonies around the drop.
disease-microscope-hint-nutrient-cross = EZ nutrient, { $cost } u. The target grows only along the cross of the drop, the rival all around it.
disease-microscope-hint-inhibitor = Phenol, { $cost } u. Scorches a 3×3 area, your cells included.
disease-microscope-hint-inhibitor-narrow = Phenol, { $cost } u. Scorches a five-cell cross.
disease-microscope-nutrient = EZ nutrient { $units } / { $capacity }
disease-microscope-inhibitor = Phenol { $units } / { $capacity }
disease-microscope-cost = −{ $cost }
disease-microscope-match-target = { $symptom }  { $count } / { $required }
disease-microscope-gauge-hint = Your colony is on the left, the rival on the right. The mark shows how many cells the stage needs right now: it covers both the quota and the required field share, so it slides right as the rival grows.
disease-microscope-gauge-growth = Your colony: { $count } cells, the stage quota is { $growth }.
disease-microscope-gauge-share = Field share: { $share }% of the required { $required }%.
disease-microscope-gauge-mark = The mark stands at { $required } cells: pass it and the stage can be closed.
disease-microscope-reservoir = Reservoir
disease-microscope-match-rival = { $count }  { $symptom }
disease-microscope-finish = Finish the stage
disease-microscope-finish-hint-ready = Quota and field share reached: the stage will close with your symptom.
disease-microscope-finish-hint-short = The colony has not reached the quota yet: the stage will not develop, only reagents will be spent.
disease-microscope-finish-hint-share = The quota is reached, but the rival holds too much of the field: the stage will not develop, only reagents will be spent.
disease-microscope-produce = Release strain
disease-microscope-output-hint = Releases the assembled genome as a strain in a vial. The blank is consumed.
disease-microscope-waiting = Processing action…
disease-microscope-request-timeout = No response received, try again.

## Operation results

disease-microscope-feedback-ready = Microscope ready. Pick a stage symptom and plate the field.
disease-microscope-feedback-prepared = The field is plated. The rival answers every move of yours.
disease-microscope-feedback-grown = Nutrient added.
disease-microscope-feedback-inhibited = The area was treated with inhibitor.
disease-microscope-feedback-forecast = The smear is stained: the rival's reply shows in the drop preview.
disease-microscope-feedback-no-forecasts = No forecasts left for this match.
disease-microscope-feedback-forecast-active = A forecast is already active until your next move.
disease-microscope-feedback-developed = The symptom has developed.
disease-microscope-feedback-reinforced = The stage gained one more symptom.
disease-microscope-feedback-advanced = The stage is closed. Moving on to the next one.
disease-microscope-feedback-no-options = Not enough free stage symptoms for a match.
disease-microscope-feedback-failed = The colony did not meet the stage conditions: it fell short of the quota or gave up too much of the field.
disease-microscope-feedback-produced = Strain released. The vial can seed a petri dish.
disease-microscope-feedback-invalid-sample = A strain blank with open stages is required.
disease-microscope-feedback-unpowered = No power.
disease-microscope-feedback-stale = The field has changed, try again.
disease-microscope-feedback-no-change = This instrument would do nothing here.
disease-microscope-feedback-no-nutrient = Not enough EZ nutrient.
disease-microscope-feedback-no-inhibitor = Not enough phenol.
disease-microscope-feedback-no-match = No match is running: plate the field first.
disease-microscope-feedback-genome-complete = The blank's genome is already complete.
disease-microscope-feedback-empty-genome = The genome has no developed symptoms yet.
